From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: galaxy-book4-edge: Split the X1E
 board and describe the EC and USB-C controllers

Split the Galaxy Book4 Edge 14 and 16 description into a SoC-independent
include, with the regulators, codec, EC, wireless devices and pinctrl,
and an X1E include with the display, speakers, USB wiring and firmware
paths, so an X1P derivative can share the common part.

Correct the hardware the first trees described: replace PMIC GLINK's
USB-C ports with the two Samsung S2MM006 controllers and connect their
endpoint graphs, add the ENE KB9058 EC with its event interface, correct
the touchscreen interrupt to GPIO 34, describe the WSA8835 speakers in
place of WSA8845 ones, enable USB-A on the 16-inch model only, and drop
the bias on the eDP HPD pin.

[birk: the state of x1-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge.dtsi,
 x1e-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge.dtsi and the 14 and 16-inch trees at
 anatase-org/patchwork 00dbccf77911, squashing 7279b3e2554, ec6b1db466c,
 aec495fc904, 9387756e896, 42a73204500, 6a1e472e1b3 and 62cdef60193;
 cbf25273f06's SPSS TPM nodes left out, since this kernel has no SPSS
 glink node; the 15-inch tree and the EL2 targets left out]

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
